   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indicators (updated in 2014)
1.1 Number of baseline surveys, evaluations and reviews conducted;
1.2 % of Project Coordination Unit (PCU) and (SPCU) State Project Coordination Unit staff  confident  doing their jobs disaggregated by gender and state.
1.3. Plan  to sustain the scheme in place
2.1 Number of young qualified graduates selected, trained and deployed disaggregated by gender and state.
2.2 % of volunteers satisfied with relevance and quality of training provided and applying at the field.
2.3 % of deployed volunteers who successfully graduate and receive certificates  (disaggregated by gender and state)
3.1	Number of community members trained and Percentage of community members who feel enabled by training disaggregated by type of training, state, age and gender
3.2	Number of start-up micro-grants awarded and number of small businesses successfully started via the micro-grants disaggregated by state, gender and age of the business owner.
3.3	Number of  small businesses successfully progressing 6 months after the start-up, disaggregated by gender of the business owner and age.
3.4	Number of environmental campaigns and cleanup exercises organised.
4.1	Number of graduation ceremonies and job fairs organised disaggregated by state;
4.2	% of deployed Youth Volunteers who successfully graduated disaggregated by state and  gender.
4.3	% of  deployed youth Volunteers employed after 6 months of training and graduation disaggregated by gender and state.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2011">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Baseline: Darfur Youth unemployment estimated = 40%</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.	Number of Technical Evaluations conducted
2.	Number of staff supported</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN"># One International Consultant and One national consultant were Recruited to support the Evaluation and preparation for next Phase &#x2013; V
# Number of Technical Evaluation ToRs and Teams prepared 
# The Evaluation was conducted late due to restrictions of COVID-19 during 2020 and the final report had been shared for comments and approval.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1.1: 300 youth volunteers selected, trained, and 95% satisfied with the training
1.1.2: 55% of youth gaining self and formal employment completion of deployment
1.1.3: 300 at-risk youth successfully completing vocational training 
1.1.4:150 youth supported to start their own businesses as entrepreneurs through business incubation

2.1.1: 15,000 community members trained in green business and environmental management disaggregated by gender
2.1.2: 50 Accumulated Savings and Credit Associations in place and functional.
2.1.3: 200 business ideas supported disaggregated by gender. 
2.2.1: 50 community infrastructure established by type

3.1.1: 300 Youth Volunteers and 1000 community Youth trained as Peace Ambassadors and Trainers (ToTs) on conflict management and negotiation skills and functional (50% female).
3.1.2: 100 locality-level peace dialogue forums and consultations organized
3.1.3: 50 peace events organized
3.1.4: At least 80 % of community members expressed an increase in social cohesion

4.1 Regular monthly coordination meetings organized with the existing State Youth Volunteer Coordination Units.
4.2 Equipment provided for key institutions of SYVCUs within 5 states of Darfur.
4.3 10 training organized for relevant key government staff on selected topics, of which 50% are female staff.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">302 youth volunteers trained and deployed to 63 communities in five Darfur states, with 43% women. More than 90% of the trainees were satisfied with the training received. The youth volunteers are yet to complete their assignments. 264 at-risk received vocational training in Central Darfur and West Darfur, with females representing 44%. 180 at-risk youth from Central Darfur and West Darfur have completed an apprenticeship program. 120 Youth have been selected to receive training and initial funding to start/scale up their business ideas.

The youth volunteers deployed into 62 communities trained 16,661 community members on green business and environmental management, with women representing 58%. 81 new ASCAs have been established with a membership of 4,719, with 54% women. ASCAs have been selected to receive support to initiate small businesses. ASCAs have been supported to register with the Ministry of Social Welfare to link up with microfinance institutions. 47 infrastructure have been prioritized and has reached various levels of completion. 

The project trained 300 youth volunteers and 720 Community Youth Volunteers on conflict management and negotiation skills, with women representing 52%. The project organized 52 peace dialogues in the targeted communities, with 15,200 people attending peace dialogues and peace events, including 48% of women in all five Darfur states. 46 CBRMs have been established in 46 communities with a total membership of 664, with women representing 24%. 46 Peace and Environment Clubs were established. 

Training needs have been identified, and 10 training sessions have been organized for 75 Government ministries staff on various topics, including M&amp;E and proposal writing. 60 meetings held by the SYCUs in the five Darfur states. Desktop computers, cameras, printers, and Tablets are being procured for the Ministry of Youth and Sports in all five Darfur states. 12 joint field monitoring conducted involving the State Youth Coordination Units.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.1	300 Youth Volunteers Selected, trained and deployed at least 50% female as community development and Peace ambassadors in 50 communities.
1.2	Vocational and Entrepreneurship training conducted for 700 Poor and marginalized youth and School drop-outs (45% female).
1.3	Startup Kits provided for the 700-trainees (45% female).
1.4	Partnerships for Apprenticeships established for at least 400 youth trainees.
1.5	300 (50% F) Youth supported in Social Enterprise Scheme through existing SMYOB Incubator using the &#x2018;&#x2019;Design Thinking&#x2019;&#x2019; and Start-up Challenge approach.
1.6	Access to Employment is facilitated using Online Platform, career fairs and linkages with employers.

2.1	50 Accumulating Saving and Credit Associations (ACSAs) established and trained with at least 1000 members of which 55% are female.
2.2	300 Youth Volunteers supported and equipped to train 15,000 community members on Green Business, and entrepreneurship and Environmental management over 3 years.
2.3	One micro-grant challenge initiated and provided business start-ups to 50 ASCAs (55% female).
2.4	Technical support and backstop provided to 50 ASCA groups on implementation of micro-grants (55%F)
2.5	Assessments and prioritization sessions conducted with communities to identify critical infrastructure gaps.
2.6	 50 critical community basic services and infrastructure established with support of Youth Volunteers.

3.1	 100 Community based conflict resolution mechanisms established.
3.2	1000 Community youth and 500 Youth Volunteers selected and trained as Youth Peace Ambassadors and ToTs on conflict management of which 50% female.
3.3	100 locality-level Peace dialogue forums organized.
3.4	100 Youth Peace and Environment Clubs established 50% of members are female.
3.5	100 peace events organized using music, dance, drama and sports.
3.6	Environmental Activities organized such as clean up exercises, tree planting and community forestry.

4.1 Regular monthly coordination meetings organized with the existing State Youth Volunteer Coordination Units.
4.2 Equipment provided for key institutions of SYVCUs within 5 states of Darfur.
4.3 10 trainings organized for relevant key government staff on selected topics of which 50% are female staff.
4.4 Technical advisory support provided to key Government ministries and departments within the states.
4.5 One Youth Empowerment Assessment conducted to inform the development of comprehensive Youth Empowerment Policy and Strategy.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project implemented peacebuilding activities in all the five Darfur states using youth ambassadors and youth volunteers. The youth volunteers and ambassadors delivered peace messages to 20,800 community members, including 45% women, through radio talk, football matches, volleyball, tug of peace, drama, traditional dance, and songs. The radio programme discussed issues related to religious hate speeches. Additionally, the youth volunteers engaged in tree planting exercises. These activities have contributed towards enhancing peaceful co-existence among communities.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
